1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Now in addition to your mindset and your personal growth and learning not far behind is going to be your daily habits and productivity.
除了心态、个人成长与学习，紧随其后的就是日常习惯和效率。

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,960
Your success is hidden in your daily routine the things that you do every day determine the person that you are going to be.
她认为，成功藏在日常作息里，每天做的事情决定你会成为怎样的人。

3
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:19,599
What is something that a lot of successful people have in common they have intentional habits.
很多成功人士有什么共同点？她的答案是，他们有刻意培养的习惯。

4
00:00:19,599 --> 00:00:24,950
That's why you see a lot of people who are successful have morning routines have night routines.
所以你会看到，很多成功人士都有晨间和晚间的固定安排。

5
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:32,720
That was the only reason why I picked up a 5 00 a m morning routine because I saw that wealthy people had morning and night routines.
我开始实行凌晨五点的晨间作息，唯一原因就是看到富有的人都有晨间和晚间习惯。

6
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:39,599
I want to be wealthy so I'm going to work on a routine I am going to change my negative habits to positive habits.
我想变得富有，所以要好好建立作息，把消极的习惯换成积极的习惯。

7
00:00:39,599 --> 00:00:46,479
Habits that fuel me habits that help me grow not habits that break me down or or destroy the life around me.
是能给我能量、帮助我成长的习惯，而不是打垮我或破坏周围生活的习惯。

8
00:00:46,479 --> 00:00:49,519
When you have a morning routine you're starting your day with intention.
有了晨间安排，你就在有意识、有目标地开启一天。

9
00:00:49,519 --> 00:00:55,839
And you don't have to get up at 5 00 a m to have a successful morning routine your morning routine should be yours.
而要拥有好的晨间安排，你不必凌晨五点起床；你的晨间安排应该适合你自己。

10
00:00:55,839 --> 00:01:03,760
That is your opportunity to start the day how you see fit that fuels you that allows you to be the best version of you throughout the day.
这是按你认为合适的方式开始一天的机会，让你得到能量，在一整天都呈现最好的自己。

11
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:10,800
You're about to go out into the world and give yourself to all of these other people and all of these other things that may not have something to do with you.
你马上就要走出去，把自己投入到其他人、其他事情中，而这些事情可能并不与自己有关。

12
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:15,760
Start your day the way that you want to start the same goes for a night routine.
用你想要的方式开始一天；晚间安排也是同样的道理。

13
00:01:15,760 --> 00:01:19,680
Ending your day the way that you want so that you can start the next day.
用自己想要的方式结束一天，这样才能迎接第二天。

14
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:24,480
You see how the domino affects how you end your day has an effect on how you start your day.
你看这就像多米诺效应，你如何结束一天，会影响如何开始新的一天。

15
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:31,440
Start your day with intention planning journaling meditating exercising whatever that may look like for you.
有意识地开启一天，可以计划、写日记、冥想、锻炼，具体做什么取决于你。

16
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:39,920
Ending your day with intention winding down so that you have quality sleep because your quality sleep affects your productivity the next day.
也有意识地结束一天，慢慢放松以获得好睡眠；她认为睡眠质量会影响第二天的效率。

17
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:47,600
Time blocking focus block out the noise if you have a task ahead you can get it done if you set aside the time to do it.
划分时间、集中注意力、屏蔽干扰；如果面前有任务，专门留出时间，你就能完成它。

18
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:53,910
Number four is health and wellness in order to have a strong mind you have to have a strong body.
第四点是健康与身心状态；她认为，要有强大的内心，也需要强健的身体。

19
00:01:53,920 --> 00:02:00,800
You have to treat your body with care if we do not take care of our bodies our bodies will break down on us especially as we age.
你得好好照顾身体；她说，如果不照顾身体，身体就会出问题，尤其随着年龄增长。

20
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:09,120
Prioritize movement nutritious food a sufficient amount of sleep when you feel good physically you naturally show up with more energy and competence.
她建议优先安排活动、营养食物和充足睡眠，并认为身体感觉好时，人自然会更有精神、更能应对事情。

21
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:14,160
You cannot pour from an empty cup prioritizing yourself is not being vain.
空杯子倒不出东西；优先照顾自己并不是虚荣。

22
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:21,030
In order for you to do for other people you have to do for yourself first fuel your body with clean nutritious healthy food.
为了能为别人付出，你得先照顾自己，用她所说的干净、营养、健康的食物给身体补充能量。

23
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:26,240
Move your body daily and you don't have to overdo it you don't have to go lift the heaviest weights in the gym.
每天动一动，也不用做过头；你不必去健身房举最重的重量。

24
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:32,720
Babe if you walk every single day you will see an improvement of your energy level getting fresh air.
亲爱的，她说如果每天走路、呼吸新鲜空气，你会感觉精力有所改善。

25
00:02:32,720 --> 00:02:36,720
You know you you're watching me right now on youtube you can pull up a yoga video.
你看，你现在就在 YouTube 看我，也可以打开一个瑜伽视频。

26
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:41,760
You could pull up an at home workout video you could pull up a stretching video move your body.
你也可以打开居家锻炼视频，或者拉伸视频，让身体活动起来。

27
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:45,750
If you neglect your body your body will neglect you eventually.
她用比喻提醒说，如果你忽视身体，身体最终也会“忽视”你。

28
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:51,519
Quality sleep it regulates your hormones it clears your mind allows your mind to operate properly.
她说，高质量睡眠会调节激素、让头脑清醒，并让思维正常运作。

29
00:02:51,519 --> 00:02:59,430
Have you ever not gotten sleep tried to get up and do something and you were just foggy like you were tired you couldn't focus you did not have the energy.
你有没有没睡够、起身想做事，却觉得脑子迷糊，疲倦、无法专注，也没精神的时候？

30
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:06,639
Treat yourself as if you are the vessel for everything else around you to to operate.
把自己当作承载周围一切正常运作的容器，好好对待自己。

31
00:03:06,639 --> 00:03:10,720
Health and wellness has to be a priority if you want to see change in your life.
她总结说，如果想看见生活发生改变，就得把健康与身心状态放在优先位置。
